    rdfs:comment "Written for this lineage. A story is Done only when each acceptance criterion has a check run in the current turn with its output saved in the repository, a verify task re-runs it from the files and not from the builder's report, and a check that cannot be run or a result that is not shown leaves the story open." .

ex:Lineage13 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 16 to 20 corrections, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl13 ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "2026-11-26: the lineage status was not advanced stage by stage while the chain was built (Mission, Scope, Goal, Objective, Backlog); the commits of 1.0.0 to 1.4.0 are the witness of that order. The status pointer (one value, moved in place) and the story and task states are moved in the next merged register, because a delta file only adds statements and a second value would break the single-value rules; until then the lineage pointer still reads Opened and every item reads Proposed.",
        "Route recorded 2026-11-26 18:57 Istanbul (Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3g, route c): the Owner ordered that after chapters 16 to 20 come chapters 21 to 25 and, after those, a return to the earliest chapters. Chapters 21 to 25 serve another purpose than the mission of this lineage (chapters 16 to 20) and can wait, so they are queued as a lineage of their own, opened only after this lineage closes; the return to the earliest chapters is queued after it. No change to the scope of this lineage." ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Achieved ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ;
    backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission13 ;
    backlog:lineageOrdinal 13 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 (sen0414-slides-lineage namespace) is the closed slides lineage this continues from, as Lineage3 to Lineage12 do."@en .

